---
# GitHub Pages serves /404.html for any unresolved path; literal permalink
# (no trailing slash) is required. Lives outside src/content/ so the directory
# data file doesn't compute a content-style permalink.
permalink: "/404.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
sitemap_enabled: false
graph_enabled: false
preview_enabled: false
page_type: top
title: 404 — signal lost
description: This frequency does not respond. The page you tried to tune to does not exist.
---
<section class="section-page section-404">
  <header class="section-header">
    <h1 class="section-title">404 // no signal</h1>
    <p class="section-description baffle-forever" aria-hidden="true">FREQUENCY_UNALLOCATED // DEAD_AIR // STATION_OFFLINE // TUNE_AGAIN</p>
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p>The frequency you tuned to does not respond. Could be the station went dark, maybe the operator got snatched by LMMC. Whatever it was, it's gone now.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <ul class="post-list section-post-list">
    {% for item in navigation %}
      <li>
        <article class="post-card">
          <h2 class="post-card-title"><a href="{{ item.url }}">{{ item.title }}</a></h2>
        </article>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
    <li>
      <article class="post-card">
        <h2 class="post-card-title"><a href="/search/">search</a></h2>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
